      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "Key=Stack,Value=Test"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0011",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Most resources can have a maximum of 50 tags. Automations can have a maximum of 5 tags.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0012",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "We recommend that you devise a set of tag keys that meets your needs for each resource type. Using a consistent set of tag keys makes it easier for you to manage your resources. You can search and filter the resources based on the tags you add. Tags don’t have any semantic meaning to and are interpreted strictly as a string of characters.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0013",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "For more information about using tags with Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud (Amazon EC2) instances, see [[p0]] in the [[p1]]Amazon EC2 User Guide[[p2]] .",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "Tag your Amazon EC2 resources"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "<em>"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "text": "</em>"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0014",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "See also: [[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "AWS API Documentation"
        }
